Barbara has a calculator which has the following keys:

$\boxed{\div}\boxed{\times}\boxed{-}\boxed{+}
\boxed{1}\boxed{2}\boxed{3}\boxed{4}
\boxed{5}\boxed{6}\boxed{7}\boxed{8}
\boxed{9}\boxed{0}
$

If she presses any digit then press any function and can only press every digit once, how many, rational or irrational, possible solutions can she get?
